1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Asta and the rest of the royal knights were busy infiltrating the Eye of the Midnight Sun's hideout.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000
While Litt, who had just revealed his true identity, was in the royal capital, engaged in a vicious battle with Julius over possession of the magic stones.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
But how? What is this strength? He's only human. He shouldn't be able to.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Using his coverless grimoire and time magic abilities, Julius managed to secure the upper hand.

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
And as the Wizard King, I'll protect the people of Clover, come what may.

9
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
However, Litt released himself from his sealing spell to launch a deadly attack on every person in the Clover Kingdom.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The big hunk of light magic. Dammit.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Now, here is your punishment, humans!

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Light magic!

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Arrows of Judgment!

14
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Time reversal magic!

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Chrono Anastasis!

16
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Stay safe!

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Julius used all the time and power he'd been saving up to protect the helpless civilians.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
But that was exactly what Litt wanted him to do.

19
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
You would have seen this attack of mine coming.

20
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
But unfortunately, you weren't able to call off that final time magic spell in order to get out of the way.

21
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Because you're...the Wizard King.

22
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
What happened to you?

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Tell me, Fungence!

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
How you love!

25
00:02:35,000 --> 00:03:04,980
Here you go.

26
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:32,440
It's a record of the absolute

27
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:46,140
You may call me Licked.

28
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,480
You're Licked?

29
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:51,720
William is lying dormant within this body.

30
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,080
That's right.

31
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:57,400
You and I both watched it through these eyes, William.

32
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,720
The end of the Wizard King.

33
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,060
What?

34
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:04,680
If that's the case, then you better say your prayers.

35
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,400
This can't be happening.

36
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:10,960
There's no way this is real.

37
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:12,940
Not Julius.

38
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:14,620
Please, no.

39
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,920
Don't just stand there, Marx.

40
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:18,900
He's injured.

41
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:21,460
Go get that quack Owen to come and heal him.

42
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:22,360
Hurry up!

43
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:23,600
Right.

44
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,240
Hang tight, Julius.

45
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:26,980
We've—

46
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:27,720
Don't bother.

47
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:31,120
He'll be gone in mere moments now.

48
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,660
You protected your kingdom to the very end.

49
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:38,780
I must commend you for that, Julius Novachrono.

50
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:42,580
But.

51
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,840
Master Lick, sir!

52
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,080
The dark magic.

53
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,200
Now dark cloaked.

54
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:54,460
Elves and humankind will never live in harmony again.

55
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:55,320
It's over.

56
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,400
Dimension Slash!

57
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:57,620
Dimension Slash!

58
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,320
He's gone.

59
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,700
Hold on, all right?

60
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,060
Don't die on me!

61
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,000
Yeah, me.

62
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:17,520
That spell you did was amazing.

63
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,800
You can cut through space itself.

64
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,460
Come on, this is no time for that stuff.

65
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:28,880
You've turned into a superb magic knight, haven't you?

66
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:33,540
Julius, like I keep telling you, I'm 28 years old.

67
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,780
I'm not some kid anymore.

68
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:41,320
It's so inspiring, seeing that your generation was raised right.

69
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,220
And knowing the next one is beginning to budge as well.

70
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,380
My own hopes.

71
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:52,460
Living on through all of the magic knights to come.

72
00:05:52,460 --> 00:06:04,580
What's wrong, Mr. Third Eye?

73
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:06,020
Running out of spells?

74
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,800
Yeah, he's finished.

75
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:13,360
No time to use fast movement or recovery magic.

76
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,800
Try another attack!

77
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,400
I dare you!

78
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:21,120
We struggled so hard to beat the Third Eye and now look!

79
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:24,500
Captain Merliona, you're so strong!

80
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:29,640
If that's really your best, I'll punch you until you're a pile of ashes!

81
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,040
Well, I guess that's it for me.

82
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,040
Now burn!

83
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,840
I'll give you one thing, Miss Royal.

84
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,520
You sure know how to pack Fiery Punch.

85
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:42,240
Which is why.

86
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:49,300
Before I burn up, I'm casting a self-destruct spell and taking you down with me!

87
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:54,120
Once you hit me, we'll disappear with a bang!

88
00:06:54,120 --> 00:07:04,760
That anti-magic brat!

89
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:09,420
He sniffed out my self-destruct spell and countered it before she landed her attack!

90
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,040
He acted so fast, it's incredible!

91
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,360
Two other people have already tried that!

92
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,880
And I'm fed up with it!

93
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,480
You can't kill yourself on my watch, you three-eyed jerk!

94
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:21,400
Got it!

95
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,880
Don't throw your life away!

96
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,000
Seriously, what's the matter with you guys?

97
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,960
You're mad at humans for taking something away from you, right?

98
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,100
I'm still fuzzy on the details!

99
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,640
But we're all people!

100
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:44,160
I want you to tell me your side of the story, and then I'm gonna tell you mine!

101
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,020
And nobody's dying until that happens, okay?

102
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,280
Good grief.

103
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:53,280
That pipsqueak really runs hard, doesn't he?

104
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:57,240
I don't recall giving you permission to butt into my fight for me!

105
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:59,180
Should I burn you as well?

106
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:03,500
He's part of the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

107
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:08,260
They've plunged the kingdom into confusion and taken a massive toll on its people.

108
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,940
They are not interested in swapping stories!

109
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:13,300
Now move!

110
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:18,460
Even if it means killing them all, we must stop them.

111
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:19,780
Yeah?

112
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,120
Why is that?

113
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:25,220
We're the same, aren't we?

114
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:27,820
So we should be able to talk things over.

115
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:31,380
Both sides are mad because we lost someone we loved.

116
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:37,800
I've been thinking a lot about this.

117
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:41,560
Everyone's fighting because we can't forgive the other side.

118
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,880
So how do we get rid of all that anger and hatred?

119
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:50,180
I know I'm not very smart, so I can't come up with the right answer.

120
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,180
But we can do it!

121
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,280
I mean, we have to, don't we?

122
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:55,820
My goal.

123
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,940
The future that I worked so hard to build.

124
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,300
I believe it isn't that far off.

125
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:05,440
Whether you're nobility, a citizen, or just a commoner.

126
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:07,580
Or even if you're not a human.

127
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:10,840
It's a future that all of you will create.

128
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:14,400
A nation that's free of hatred and prejudice.

129
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:19,840
I just want a kingdom where all of us get along and laugh together.

130
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,520
And when I'm the Wizard King, we'll have one.

131
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:23,540
You'll see.

132
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:27,220
You imbecile.

133
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:30,320
Proudly proclaiming something so outrageous.

134
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,400
I think he's actually serious.

135
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:39,600
In fact, it reminds me of what someone else said once before.

136
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:43,280
This little one here is the key to our future.

137
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:46,100
The bridge that will unite the elves and humankind.

138
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,600
Congratulations, Licta Tetya.

139
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:49,660
Congratulations!

140
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:54,300
If only the rest of the human race thought about it the way these guys do.

141
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:55,600
Then maybe...

142
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:58,100
No.

143
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,300
It's too late to stop now.

144
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:09,760
Hey, welcome back!

145
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,360
Took you long enough.

146
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:14,160
You snagged the last of the magic stones, right?

147
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,240
Watch your tongue, Radies.

148
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:18,320
Everything went as we planned.

149
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:19,840
In fact, even better.

150
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:23,040
Our Master Lict has assassinated the Wizard King.

151
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,040
Seriously?

152
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,020
That's awesome!

153
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,380
Wow, Master Lict!

154
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:27,340
Great going!

155
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,140
The time has come.

156
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:33,560
There's not a soul who can stand in our way anymore.

157
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:42,840
Come on.

158
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,460
Just a little longer.

159
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,260
When Owen gets here, he's gonna fix you right up.

160
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,700
That leader was so powerful.

161
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:55,180
He could have easily killed everyone in the land.

162
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:58,260
Even without collecting all of the magic stones.

163
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:02,160
That means he must be after something else.

164
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:07,540
I fear that Clover Kingdom may yet suffer a devastating fate.

165
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,680
I let him steal the stones.

166
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,400
I'm sorry.

167
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:18,680
Such a failure is below the Wizard King.

168
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,260
Forget that.

169
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:23,040
You just saved thousands of lives.

170
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:25,740
I hope we make it to him in time.

171
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:32,200
Marks is going to be so disappointed in me for the way things ended.

172
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:38,400
It's a shame that I won't be there when Vigolion finally wakes up.

173
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:40,540
Yami.

174
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,300
There are still so many things.

175
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:45,820
Things I wanted to tell you.

176
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:48,400
Don't go talking like that.

177
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,340
You can't check out on me now.

178
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:52,480
That's something I can't forgive.

179
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:55,100
Because I still haven't...

180
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:57,160
Look at that freak.

181
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:59,120
He's not from here, you know.

182
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:01,080
He washed up from some other country.

183
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:02,640
Lives alone on the coast.

184
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:05,620
I wish he'd just go back where he belongs.

185
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:07,620
Wow!

186
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:09,900
Was that dark magic?

187
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,580
What the...

188
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:13,680
Awesome!

189
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,300
I've never seen it before.

190
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:18,400
Please, you've got to let me get a closer look.

191
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:19,420
Yeah, no.

192
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:20,400
Who are you, mister?

193
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:21,940
I...

194
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:24,500
Oh, well, I'm no one to be suspicious of.

195
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:27,640
I assure you, I'm just a magic knight captain out walking in disguise.

196
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:29,620
What's a magic knight, captain?

197
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,240
Huh?

198
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,460
You don't know that?

199
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:32,540
Okay.

200
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:38,540
Why don't you come with me and I'll show you?

201
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,980
I think you have real potential.

202
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:41,860
See this, Yami?

203
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,700
It's how you write your name here.

204
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:44,800
Oh, great.

205
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:48,180
I'm never going to remember a bunch of squiggly lines like that.

206
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,720
Well, if you practice, you'll pick it up in no time.

207
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,060
I don't want to.

208
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:53,440
Aww.

209
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:56,280
But if you learn to write, I'll buy dinner for you.

210
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,080
I'm on it.

211
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:02,180
You haven't been on the squad for very long.

212
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:05,160
But I'm already astonished by everything you've accomplished.

213
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,920
That said, I'd rather you didn't run too wild.

214
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:09,440
We've had some, well...

215
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:09,780
Uh-oh.

216
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:10,320
Look.

217
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:11,540
It's the enemy.

218
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,140
Then let's go.

219
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,120
But reel it in a little.

220
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:15,600
Yeah!

221
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:19,900
Well, we'll work on that later.

222
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:25,500
And Yami, from this moment on, you will be recognized as founder and leader of the Black Bulls.

223
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:27,340
Best of luck, captain.

224
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:36,920
Yami, I'm leaving the rest to you now.

225
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:51,760
Yes, sir.

226
00:13:51,760 --> 00:14:05,220
I got to meet so many people and see so many spells.

227
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:13,640
It was a fun life.

228
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:17,280
A good life.

229
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:24,160
Julius.

230
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:24,380
Julius.

231
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:34,800
Don't you worry, friend.

232
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,800
We'll keep the kingdom safe for you.

233
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:44,640
I can't help but wonder how everyone's doing.

234
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:48,860
I've been casting my spatial jamming spell for several hours.

235
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,740
It's getting rather difficult to hold my arms up.

236
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,420
But this is no time for complaining.

237
00:14:56,200 --> 00:15:00,980
The Royal Knights are in there battling the Eye of the Midnight Sun with everything they've got.

238
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:04,440
The future of the Clover Kingdom hangs in the balance.

239
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,020
Please, team.

240
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,840
Do your very best.

241
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:12,880
Hey!

242
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:13,900
Look up there!

243
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:15,060
What's that?

244
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,240
It's an abundance of mana!

245
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,640
We're headed straight for the center.

246
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:23,000
You guys, be careful!

247
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:25,260
I don't care who crosses us.

248
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:26,820
I'm not in the mood to lose.

249
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,540
Neither am I!

250
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,780
Let's go knock them dead, you know!

251
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:42,040
This place is so bizarre.

252
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:42,620
Yes.

253
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,240
Is that a person?

254
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,320
The mana.

255
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,560
It's so...

256
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:01,060
Yes.

257
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,300
It's unbelievably powerful.

258
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:19,120
All it needs now is the last of the magic stones.

259
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:25,120
We'll awaken our true might with the Monument of the Tree of Life to guide our every step.

260
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:26,680
Yes.

261
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:31,000
The fateful day that we've waited for has arrived.

262
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:37,000
Yeah, since we were lucky enough to be chosen by the mana, our magic powers are about to go through the roof!

263
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:37,620
Ha!

264
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:39,220
This is gonna be fun!

265
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:43,140
Those magic knights will be dead before they even figure out what hit them!

266
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:47,060
With our new power, plus my dark magic items will be unbeatable!

267
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:49,200
Oh, I can hardly wait!

268
